{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## rebar-debug report — resolve_project None sentinel (scenario 4)\n\n**Problem** — Live DC rehearsal scenario 4 (`test_absent_project_resolves_to_legacy_default`)\nfails at `assert 0 == 1`: a no-flag ticket never lands in the legacy project.\n\n**Proven root cause** — `resolve_project` (`projects_store.py`) treated the tri-state\n`bridge_project` field's present-but-null `None` (the reducer's seeded \"absent/legacy\"\nsentinel, cef7 `_state.py:53-58`) as never-sync by lumping it into `if not value: return None`,\nalongside the explicit `\"\"`. Because the reducer ALWAYS materializes `bridge_project=None` for a\nno-flag create, the old `\"bridge_project\" not in ticket` branch was dead, so `legacy_default`\nnever fired for the cohort it exists to serve → the outbound create gate (`outbound_differ.py:584`\n`if not target: return`) dropped the create.\n\n**Proof** — runtime-confirmed discriminating experiment:\n`resolve_project({\"bridge_project\": None}, ld=\"LEG\")` → `None` vs. explicit `\"LEG\"` → `\"LEG\"`\nand `\"\"` → `None`. `git blame a22e6f3642` confirms original defect, not a regression.\n\n**Legitimacy: `defect`** — violates the authoritative cef7 tri-state contract\n(`reducer/_state.py:53-58`): `None` = absent/legacy → must route to `legacy_default`.\n\n**Caller-dependency gate: CLEARED** — single production caller (`outbound_differ.py:584`) is the\nmalfunctioning site itself; no existing test pins `None`→None (all 15 projects-store /\nensure-mapping tests stay green). Outbound create is double-guarded (mapping seeded AND\n`legacy_default` set and a mapping key) — the only behavior change is the designed cef7 legacy\nmigration.\n\n**Test** — held-out RED unit test\n`test_resolve_project_null_sentinel_routes_to_legacy_default` in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_projects_store_heldout.py`, seen RED (`assert None == 'REB'`)\nbefore the fix, GREEN after; teeth proven by defect-seeded mutation (reintroducing\n`if not value` returns it to RED). Scenario 4 strengthened with a positive\n`legacy in _planned_projects(preview)` assertion (the old `_assert_scope` was vacuous on an\nempty plan).\n\n**Fix** — `resolve_project` rewritten to distinguish the three states explicitly:\n`None`/absent → `legacy_default`, `\"\"` → `None`, non-empty → verbatim (docstring updated).\n\n**Siblings** — construct sweep: the `if not value` truthiness-collapse of a tri-state is the\nclass; `resolve_project` was its only live instance (single caller, single resolution site).\nParity sweep: the rule \"the None absent/legacy sentinel routes to legacy_default\" is enforced at\nthe single shared resolution core both transports call — no parallel surface bypasses it. None\nfound.\n\n**Fix-safety** — restoration (not creation), no new dependency, no test weakened.\n\n**Landed** — Gerrit change 1810 (pushed; awaiting LLM-Review +1 + Verified +1).\n\n**Replication** — pending: a live `Live External Integration` DC rehearsal run must show\nscenario 4 green end-to-end (AC #4) before this closes."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786787191362797001,"uuid":"6e47c79d-ed17-4864-8758-936245564726"}